{
  "title": "ArcCivs permission-gated settlement testing mode (planned)",
  "assumptions": [
    "This assessment models only the incremental automatic construction-material item flow when the new test-mode option is off versus on. Existing administrative/Creative item grants continue in both states and are not treated as zero total item issuance. That existing grant capability can export physical items; any resale remains unpriced.",
    "Task-fixed target contract, not verified source or runtime behavior: new permission arccivs.testing defaults false; only a city owner may enable immortality (autoHP at least 1) and automatic construction materials (default off). Existing arccivs.chunkload remains a per-city toggle with legacy default on. The GrocerMC test-city owner explicitly requests all three city toggles on. Owner permission is cached with a 15-second refresh and 30-second allowance; losing permission stops new material grants and immortality.",
    "Automatic material grants fill only the actual deficit for the current construction order after existing construction storage and builder inventory are counted. Items enter the real builder bag through a durable inventory receipt. The bag has 27 slots with native stack limits. Recovery does not replay or reissue a completed grant. Ordinary cities keep the new testing options off.",
    "Low/base/high are illustrative 1/2/4 test operators and 1/4/12 accepted deficit-filling grants per operator-day, at 64 mixed vanilla items per grant. These are sensitivity assumptions, not telemetry, a guaranteed quantity, an enforced daily allowance, or a lifetime cap. Cumulative administrative item mint has no imposed lifetime cap.",
    "Vault, premium tokens, and player XP are separate units; the direct delta for each is zero. The item flow is counted as individual items only; there is no item-to-currency conversion. The existing Creative/admin path can export physical items into possible monetization paths, but no material-specific sale price or normal-player income is inferred, and the planned SELL-to-contract transition is not assumed active.",
    "Immortality preserves existing possessions and internal resident skill that could otherwise be lost on death; this is preservation, not new item issuance, and its frequency/value is unknown. A movement fix may restore realized work throughput without changing per-cycle output or reward quantity; any throughput change is unmeasured.",
    "Fresh read-only ARC Economy V2 query: 168 hours, economy_server=survival, generatedAt=1792749707988 (2026-10-23T10:01:47.988Z), since=1792144907986 (2026-10-16T10:01:47.986Z). The exact window excluded 0 boundary-crossing and 0 future records/operations. Coverage: 2,665 records, 31,040 operations, 22 players. This is background ledger context, not ArcCivs/test-mode attribution.",
    "The queried typed ledger reported Vault 685959.9553100035 minted and 1522950.11 burned; tokens 51 minted and 0 burned. One Vault source/origin was unclassified (1 record, 1 operation, absolute amount 5000); source coverage was not perfect. Legacy mixed-currency totals are ignored. The MCP clamps economy_limit to 100; no material-specific shop selection or concentration-group query was made, and ranked/top-account views are not used as complete evidence."
